---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import HeroShapes from '../components/HeroShapes.astro';
import { FRANK_REF, SITE, pageUrl } from '../i18n/ui';
import { offer } from '../i18n/offer';
import Doors from '../components/Doors.astro';

const c = offer.en;
import '../styles/framework.css';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'The 5 Levels of AI Fluency',
  description:
    'A map of how AI shows up in your work, from better questions to a system that runs in the background. For figuring out where you actually want to sit.',
  inLanguage: 'en',
  url: pageUrl('en', 'framework'),
  image: `${SITE}/og/framework-en.png`,
  author: FRANK_REF,
};
---

<Layout
  title="The Five Levels of AI | Franksy"
  description="A map of how AI shows up in your work, from better questions to a system that runs in the background. For figuring out where you actually want to sit."
  locale="en"
  pathKey="framework"
  ogType="article"
  ogImage="/og/framework-en.png"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <HeroShapes />
    <div class="container hero-inner">
      <div class="hero-text">
        <p class="eyebrow">A reflective framework</p>
        <h1 class="display">The 5 Levels of <em>AI Fluency.</em></h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">Five levels of fluency. Each more advanced than the last, and the right one depends on the work in front of you.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section intro">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="prose measure">
        <p>AI gets pitched as transformation. Most of what people actually want from it is quieter: <strong>a way to do the same work with less mental weight, and more room for what matters.</strong></p>

        <p>Most people use AI at one level for some kinds of work, and another for others. That's normal. The right level depends on what you're trying to do. But the further you go, the more these tools become part of how you actually think.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="marker marker--square" aria-hidden="true"></span>The five levels</div>
      <h2 class="h1 section-title">Each builds on what came before.</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">{c.levels.lead}</p>

      <div class="levels">
        {c.levels.items.map((level) => (
          <div class="level">
            <div class="level-num">{level.num}</div>
            <div class="level-content">
              <div class="level-name">{level.name}</div>
              <div class="level-headline">{level.who}</div>
              <div class="level-desc"><span class="level-label">{c.labels.example}</span> {level.example}</div>
              <div class="level-desc level-sign"><span class="level-label">{c.labels.sign}</span> {level.sign}</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="section gap-wrap">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="marker marker--square" aria-hidden="true"></span>Orientation</div>
      <h2 class="h1 section-title">Where most people are, and where it gets interesting.</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">Two different relationships with AI. Most people are in the first one, not because the second is hard, but because they haven't seen what it looks like from the inside.</p>

      <div class="gap-grid">
        <div class="gap-card stuck">
          <div class="gap-stat">80%</div>
          <div class="gap-sub">of professionals</div>
          <div class="gap-headline">Treat AI as a tool.</div>
          <div class="gap-body">Use it occasionally, for one-off questions. Like a faster search engine. Helpful, but the work mostly stays the same shape, done in mostly the same way.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="gap-card ahead">
          <div class="gap-stat">20%</div>
          <div class="gap-sub">work alongside AI</div>
          <div class="gap-headline">Treat AI as a thinking partner.</div>
          <div class="gap-body">It holds the context of their projects. Captures their meetings. Pushes back on their ideas. It becomes part of how they think. Not just something they consult.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cost-block">
        <div class="cost-label eyebrow">What changes when you cross over</div>
        <div class="cost-items">
          <div class="cost-item">
            <div class="cost-amount">More room</div>
            <div class="cost-desc">Not because you work less. It's because you stop carrying what doesn't need carrying.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="cost-item">
            <div class="cost-amount">Things move</div>
            <div class="cost-desc">Projects you've been holding. Decisions you've been putting off. They start having a place to happen.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section band reflection">
    <div class="container reflection-inner">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="marker marker--square" aria-hidden="true"></span>{c.thread.eyebrow}</div>
      <h2 class="h1 section-title">{c.thread.title}</h2>
      {c.thread.paragraphs.map((p) => <p>{p}</p>)}
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section" id="doors">
    <div class="container">
      <Doors locale="en" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section sting">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="tagline sting-text">Less clutter. <em>More presence.</em><br />That's the work.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="booking-section">
    <div class="container">
      <p>Ready when you are.</p>
      <a href="https://app.cal.com/franksy/connect" class="btn btn-primary" data-cal-link="franksy/connect" data-cal-namespace="connect" data-cal-config='{"layout":"month_view","useSlotsViewOnSmallScreen":"true"}'>Book a 15-minute call</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
